WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.553
Today, I'm going to show you how to add a Persistent Disk to your Linux VM

00:00:04.553 --> 00:00:08.854
Open the Google Developer's Console, and go to the  'VM Instances' screen.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:09.820
Click the instance

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.560
Scroll down to the 'Additional disks' section

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.440
Click 'Edit', now click 'Add item', 'Select a Disk', 'Create new Disk'

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.820
Now, give it a Name, select the Type, choose 'Blank Disk', specify the size, and click 'Create'

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:25.140
Now click save

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.300
Now SSH into your machine

00:00:27.585 --> 00:00:30.925
Get the name of the disk by using the 'lsblk' command

00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:33.345
Now make a new directory to mount your disk.

00:00:33.345 --> 00:00:36.956
Now, we can use the 'safe_format_and_mount' tool to mount the disk

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:42.165
Specify the disk name, and the name of the directory we just created, and hit enter

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:45.139
In a few minutes, the disk is formatted and mounted!

00:00:45.139 --> 00:00:49.762
We can use the 'lsblk' command again to see the disk is correctly mounted

